## Configure Slurm

Similarly, we can configure Slurm and import the cryptographic key that is
required by the *munge* authentication library to be available on every host in
the resource management pool. The key goes in the `secrets` runtime overlay,
which warewulfd serves only to root on the nodes. Issue the following:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
```bash
# Configure Slurm server in the overlay (using "configless" option)
# using a tag in a template file (slurmd.ww)
wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig \
 /opt/ohpc/pub/examples/slurm/slurmd.ww /etc/sysconfig/slurmd.ww

# Set the value of the slurmctld tag to the $sms_ip for the nodes profile.
wwctl profile set --yes nodes --tagadd slurmctld="${sms_ip}"

# Configure munge: the key in the runtime overlay, readable by munge only
wwctl overlay import --parents secrets /etc/munge/munge.key
wwctl overlay chown secrets /etc/munge/munge.key "$(id -u munge):$(id -g munge)"
wwctl overlay chown secrets /etc/munge "$(id -u munge):$(id -g munge)"
wwctl overlay chmod secrets /etc/munge 0700
wwctl overlay chmod secrets /etc/munge/munge.key 0400

# Start munge after wwclient has applied the runtime overlay (munge key)
wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig \
	/opt/ohpc/admin/warewulf/wait-wwclient.conf \
	/etc/systemd/system/munge.service.d/wait-wwclient.conf
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
